  "question": "Background / Context\nThe global gaming market is a significant industry, projected to surpass $300 billion by 2027. With substantial financial incentives, major game publishers aim to create highly successful video games. Evaluating whether games are improving over time or if the best years have passed is crucial for understanding industry trends.\n\n Objectives\nThe project aims to analyze the popularity trends in video games by examining the top 400 best-selling games from 1977 to 2020. By comparing game sales data with both critic and user reviews, the goal is to identify the best years for video games in terms of sales and rating.\n\n Stakeholders & Users\n- Game Publishers: Interested in understanding market trends and historical performance.\n- Developers: Seek insights into critical success factors in game development.\n- Industry Analysts: Explore the data to provide market forecasting and insights.\n- Gamers and Enthusiasts: Interested in historical trends and peak years in gaming.\n\n Functional Descriptions\n1. Data Analysis: Examine the dataset of game sales, critic scores, and user scores for the top 400 best-selling games.\n2. Comparison of Years: Analyze and compare the years based on average critic and user reviews.\n3. Identification of Peak Years: Identify the years with the highest average scores, considering criteria such as sales volume and number of high-scoring games.\n\n Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Data Accuracy: Ensure the integrity and accuracy of datasets used for analysis.\n- Efficiency: Optimize data processing for handling datasets from 1977 to 2020 efficiently.\n- Usability: Provide clear and accessible results for stakeholders to derive insights easily.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0216\nCREATE TABLE `video_games` (\n  `game_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `platform` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `release_year` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `genre` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `publisher` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `na_sales` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `eu_sales` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `jp_sales` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `other_sales` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `global_sales` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `critic_score` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `user_score` decimal(3,1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`game_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
